# No patches — proper implementation only

Owner standing order: **do not patch around problems.**

If something is wrong, fix it at the **owning layer** with a real, durable implementation that matches the product contract. Do not leave paper-over hacks in the NEW app (or anywhere else).

## Forbidden (patches)

- Client shims that hide wrong or missing server responses
- Silent `catch` / ignore on auth, wallet, gifts, IAP, LiveKit, upload, or realtime paths
- Fake success, stub success, or “treat any 2xx as OK” without checking the real response contract
- Extra alias listeners / dual code paths “just in case” instead of aligning to the real event/API name
- Local-only state that pretends a production payment, session, or live join succeeded
- Feature-flag spaghetti or temporary branches left as the permanent fix
- Restoring deleted owner files / reversing intentional deletes without being asked
- “Quick” workarounds that lie to users or the backend

## Required (proper fix)

1. Identify the **owner** (auth store, `roomSocket`, `LiveKitSession`, `feedApi`, IAP verify path, etc.)
2. Fix **there** so the contract is honest: types, lifecycle, cleanup, success/failure
3. Align client to the **real** production API/WS/LiveKit contract (reference OLD behaviour/server, do not invent)
4. Fail visibly with correct errors when the real path fails
5. Prefer the smallest change that is still **complete and correct** — not the smallest hack

## Audit vs fix

- When asked to audit: report findings; **do not silently patch** while auditing
- When asked to fix: implement properly at the owning layer, or stop and state the external blocker
- Never call a patch “done”

## Default

**No patches. Proper implementation only.**
